# Build artifacts that must never enter the build context.
#
# The rust-builder stage copies whole submodule directories (rather than named
# files) so the image still BUILDS when the submodules are not checked out — a
# missing file makes COPY fail, an empty directory does not. Copying the whole
# directory would otherwise drag in ~300 MB of host-built target/ per tool: an
# accidental cache-buster on every local build, and a pile of stale glibc
# objects shipped into a musl builder for no reason.
sources/*/target/
sources/*/*/target/

# Never useful in an image build, always large.
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
.git/modules/

# Generated locally by `make rust-dist` / `make agent-dist`; the image builds
# its own inside the builder stages and must not inherit a host copy, which
# could be a different architecture or an older submodule commit.
rust-dist/
agent-dist/
